=21879"},"modified":"2022-05-16T11:56:09","modified_gmt":"2022-05-16T09:56:09","slug":"basic-authentication-deprecation","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.derdack.com\/basic-authentication-deprecation\/","title":{"rendered":"Basic Authentication in Exchange Online ends"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>In <a href=\"https:\/\/techcommunity.microsoft.com\/t5\/exchange-team-blog\/basic-authentication-and-exchange-online-february-2021-update\/ba-p\/2111904\">February 2021<\/a> Microsoft announced that basic authentication would be deprecated some time in the second half of 2021) but extended the deadline due to popular demand. Just a couple of days ago Microsoft announced that the final deadline for the Basic Authentication is <a href=\"https:\/\/techcommunity.microsoft.com\/t5\/exchange-team-blog\/basic-authentication-deprecation-in-exchange-online-may-2022\/ba-p\/3301866\">October 1<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>But why are we posting about this here? Well, the Enterprise Alert E-Mail Module does support Basic Authentication for on-prem and Online Exchange and the authentication method is most likely still used by some.<\/p>\n<p>We strongly recommend you to switch your Online exchange integration from Basic Authentication to more secure authentication method like OAuth.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/derdack.zendesk.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/360047391234-Setting-up-OAuth-for-office-365\">Setting up OAuth for office 365 \u2013 Derdack (zendesk.com)<\/a><\/p>\n<p>If you do struggle or have further questions please feel free to reach out to our Derdack support team under <a href=\"mailto:support@derdack.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">support@derdack.com<\/a>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>In February 2021 Microsoft announced that basic authentication would be deprecated some time in the second half of 2021) but extended the deadline due to popular demand. Just a couple of days ago Microsoft announced that the 